## AI Writing Tells to Avoid (2025-2026)

**Why this matters**: 74% of recruiters claim to identify AI-generated resumes; 53% have reservations about AI content; 20% consider it disqualifying. Detection tools (Winston AI, GPTZero) now exceed 95% accuracy by analyzing "perplexity" (predictability) and "burstiness" (sentence length variation).

---

### Flagged Words - Do Not Use

**Why flagged**: Academic studies (PubMed 2020-2024, FSU 2025) tracked word frequency before/after ChatGPT release. These words showed statistically significant spikes—some 10x+ increase—making them reliable AI signatures. Detectors weight these heavily.

| Category | Words | Why problematic |
|----------|-------|-----------------|
| LLM favorites | delve, underscore, meticulous, commendable, notable | Rare in human writing pre-2023; now hallmarks of AI |
| Filler intensifiers | pivotal, crucial, vital, undoubtedly, arguably | AI hedges by making everything sound important |
| Abstract metaphors | tapestry, landscape, realm, paradigm, framework | AI avoids specifics; these let it sound meaningful without saying anything |
| Corporate buzzwords | leverage, optimize, harness, robust, dynamic, elevate, foster, catalyst, seamlessly, strategically | AI trained on business content over-indexes on MBA-speak |
| Resume clichés | comprehensive, intricate, garner, boast, surpass, embark | Generic achievement language that could apply to anyone |

---

### Flagged Phrases - Do Not Use

**Why flagged**: AI generates safe, non-committal, universally-applicable text. These phrases pad word count without adding information—a pattern detectors recognize.

| Phrase type | Examples | Why problematic |
|-------------|----------|-----------------|
| Empty descriptors | "results-driven professional," "dynamic self-starter," "team player" | Says nothing specific; could describe anyone |
| Hedging intros | "It's important to note," "It's worth mentioning" | AI's way of introducing points without committing to them |
| Grandiose framing | "Navigate the complexities," "In the fast-paced world of," "Rich tapestry of," "Embark on a journey" | AI compensates for lack of real detail with dramatic language |
| Formal transitions | "Furthermore," "Moreover," "Additionally" as sentence starters | Human writers rarely start sentences this way; feels like a term paper |
| Scope inflation | "A wide range of," "comprehensive suite of" | Vague scale claims instead of specifics |

---

### Structural Red Flags

**Why flagged**: Detectors measure "burstiness"—humans naturally vary sentence length and structure. AI produces unnaturally consistent patterns.

| Pattern | Why it signals AI |
|---------|-------------------|
| Uniform sentence length | Humans mix short punchy statements with longer explanations. AI averages out. |
| Overly formal tone | No contractions, no personality. AI defaults to safe/neutral. |
| Generic accomplishments | "Improved efficiency" without numbers, project names, or context. AI can't invent specifics. |
| Over-explanation | AI explains obvious things because it doesn't know what readers already understand. |
| Perfect parallel structure | Every bullet starting with past-tense verb, same rhythm. Too consistent. |
| Keyword stuffing | AI optimizes for ATS by cramming terms unnaturally. Recruiters notice. |
| Hedging verbs | "helped to," "assisted with," "contributed to"—AI avoids claiming direct ownership. |

---

### What Passes as Human

**Why this works**: These patterns have low perplexity (unexpected) and high burstiness (varied), which detectors associate with human writing.

| Pattern | Why it reads as human |
|---------|----------------------|
| Specific numbers, dates, project names | AI can't fabricate real details; specificity signals authenticity |
| Imperfect but clear phrasing | Minor awkwardness is human; AI is too polished |
| Industry shorthand/acronyms | "K8s," "CI/CD," "P0 incident"—jargon AI uses cautiously |
| Concrete actions + measurable outcomes | "Reduced deploy time from 45min to 8min" not "optimized deployment processes" |
| Occasional sentence fragments | Bullets don't need to be complete sentences. AI over-formalizes. |
| Natural voice | How you'd actually explain the work to a colleague |
